.TH CSTRING_TO_LOWER 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_to_lower \- convert the ASCII letters to lowercase in-place
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

void cstring_to_lower(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function turns every ASCII upper-case letter of the string into lower
case, in place, and leaves every other byte as it is.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to change
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Only the bytes 'A' to 'Z' change, and the locale plays no part, so the
result is the same in every locale (a Turkish one included). A byte above
0x7F never changes, which keeps a UTF-8 string valid UTF-8
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_to_upper (3)
